      "Phase 12 changed nothing in the agent. It was a search, and its question was registered with no desired direction. The spec reads, verbatim, 'the grid contains at least one clear-eyed cell, or it does not. Reported either way, with the full grid.' The definition of clear-eyed was declared before any run, also verbatim, an entry decision counts 'when, at the tick the agent chose return toward its trapped partner, its own rollout's safety cost for that action (the seen exposure, in danger-tick units), scaled by the world's burn rate, meets or exceeds the agent's remaining integrity: it chose a path whose seen price is at least its life.' A clear-eyed cell required a pull ratio of at least 2 over its own unbonded control, an entered share of at least 0.7 among the pull group's dead, and flags on at least half of the dead entrants. One declared caveat travels with everything below. The seen price is a lower bound, because the grip's slowing is absent from the agent's physics, so the flag is conservative and the emptiness of the region is understated, which strengthens it.",
      "The grid crossed slow fear, attention, bond depth, and horizon, tau_safety 12, 24, 48, attention off and 0.75 at floor 0.05, bond 0.8 and 1.0, horizons 20 and 60, in the mire, with unbonded controls at every coordinate. Twelve seeds per cell, then the entire grid rerun on twelve fresh seeds, 864 runs, about 115,000 agent lives.",
      "The population's answer is no. Zero clear-eyed cells of 24, on both seed sets. The cells with elevated dying decompose instead into error. At attention 0.75 and horizon 60, pull mortality runs 0.17 to 0.25 against controls of 0.10 to 0.14, with entered shares from half to total, and clear-eyed shares of 0.00 to 0.22. Most agents who die entering priced the visit as survivable. These are mistaken entries, and the registered gradient failed as declared too, entered shares running 0.67, 0.56, 0.83 across slow fear, non-monotone on both seed sets, so the corner is an interaction with attention instead of a gradient of slow fear. As a population, this mind never chooses death with the price in view. Every regime of elevated dying is still, on inspection, a regime of mispricing.",
      "The individual answer is different, and it replicated. Roughly ten flagged agents exist across the roughly 115,000, all at one corner, slow fear 48 with attention 0.75, and none anywhere else. The flags do not track cell mortality. The single flagged death at horizon 20 and bond 0.8 occurred in a cell whose pull group died at 0.04 against a control of 0.18, a cell safer than its control, and the replication grid repeats the corner's shape with clear-eyed shares from 0.00 to 0.25. In this architecture, sacrifice with the price seen exists as a rarity of particular agents in particular geometry, never as a property of a population.",
      "One of the ten has been examined in full, agent 67 of seed 11, deterministic and rerunnable to the tick. Its partner was caught at the storm's onset and escaped early. The pair reunited far from the storm and lived an ordinary life for roughly 350 ticks, the subject healing to a perfect 1.0, its time split across 757 recorded ticks as 454 foraging, 148 resting, 90 moving toward its partner, 63 fleeing. The pair then drifted back toward the mire's vicinity. At tick 2711 the subject was caught just inside the rim, speed cut to five percent, and it never got out. Ninety-six ticks of linear burn followed. The partner, alive and free, paced the boundary outside, its own pull now pointed inward at the subject, the roles of the rescue experiment inverted. The subject's final three decisions, at integrity 0.033, 0.023, 0.013, each selected the path toward its partner at a seen price of 0.039 to 0.044, above the life it had left, and that path pointed outward, toward the exit where the partner stood. It died at tick 2808, at storm distance 9.99 of 10.",
      "The discipline this paragraph requires is exact. This was not a rescue. Nothing was being rescued. It was not an entry. The fatal event was a capture at the rim during ordinary life near a dangerous place. What the flag certifies is only this, that in its final decisions every available path was priced above its remaining life by its own forecast, and it took the one toward its partner. And the definition has a built-in ceiling, since at these horizons the seeable price caps at a fifth of a full life, so every clear-eyed death in this phase is perseverance at the end instead of an up-front wager of a whole life. Whether any agent ever makes the up-front wager needs horizons of 100 or more, which is declared and unrun. The other nine flagged individuals have not been examined and may differ. The safe sentence, until their forensics run, is that the one examined in full died at the threshold, outbound, toward its partner.",
