      "A bereaved agent is one whose partner died while it still lived, and a dead partner sits at infinite distance, where separation distress equals the bond exactly. A neglect death is a bereaved agent later found dead with its energy at zero. At kappa 0, no bereaved agent starved, none of 61. At kappa 2, 79 of 556 starved at bond 0.4 and 87 of 618 at bond 0.8, which is 14.2 and 14.1 percent, while starvation among partnered agents whose partners survived was 0.000 in every attention cell. Grief at kappa 0 is a weight that fades without consequence. Grief at kappa 2 is a weight that silences hunger until energy runs out. The middle of the map is nearly empty, and the emptiness is itself a result. At moderate sharpness the storm killed almost nobody, so almost nobody was bereaved, because once fear leads it owns the mind and evacuation is near total. That reading is an inference from bereaved counts in this arena rather than a separately designed experiment. Across the two arenas the same parameter saves the acute crisis and kills the everyday.",
